  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best result is config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat; acc=0.715). All multimodal experiments tested so far used concat fusion, so the effect of fusion strategy is completely unexplored. Config_037 changes only the fusion method from concat to weighted, holding all other settings identical to config_036. This is a clean single-variable experiment that directly tests whether a learned weighted combination of modalities can outperform simple concatenation. Given that the image modality alone is weak (best 0.33) while RNA is strong (0.65), the optimal weighting between modalities may differ substantially from an equal-weight concat, making this a high-information experiment. If weighted fusion improves performance, it confirms that modality importance is asymmetric and guides further tuning; if it does not, it confirms concat is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward other untested dimensions (e.g., transformer aggregation with scvi in multimodal)."
}

